A||||4||mshill||Fieros at the boneyards today...||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||08-10-2000||08:44 PM||||I made the rounds today and hit two of the three Pick-n-Pulls and one other self serve boneyard in the Sacramento, CA area.  There is an enourmous number of Fieros showing up these days.  I saw/scavenged from no less than 20 cars.  This is way up from the usual of 2-3 per yard.<P>Here's what I saw:<P>1 - 88 4 Cyl Coupe<BR>1 - 86 GT<BR>1 - 86 SE 6 Cyl<P>The rest were 84-87 4 cylinder coupes.  There were many with some decent interior pieces.  I had already scavenged most of the good stuff from the GT and the other V6s. Good coupe body parts are plentiful.  <P>One yard had nine coupes all lined up.  From the very last one I scored 1" front sway bar, 7/8" rear sway bar, lowering springs, and a pair of Koni shocks (see the mall for the shocks).  I have not decided what I will be doing with the bars and springs yet.<P>I saw one coupe whose drivers side front end was totally crushed, but the drivers footwell and steering wheel area were completely intact.  Most of those headon impact test show the drivers footwellbeing crushed, but not this Fiero.  I was impressed.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-11-2000||01:46 AM||||If you decide to get rid of the lowering springs anytime soon, let me know.  I'm looking for a set for the Grape Ape, but just can't quite afford the going price.  How do you know they're lowering springs?||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||08-11-2000||02:19 AM||||and, let me know about the sway bars -- my '87GT is kinda squirelly!! (When I was out there George - at the Fiero Shop in Hayward - and I talked about lowering springs, KYB's and sway bars.........think I might do the sway bar (on the rear) first and then go from there........By the way, did you go on the Wine Run with GGF when they went to Calistoga? I missed it but heard it was great fun!! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||08-11-2000||09:38 AM||||Monkey, The dead giveaway on the springs was how the rear springs were loose on the strut perches.  That combined with the sway bars and the Konis, I figured it was at one time a complete suspension package.  Still have not decided whether to keep or not.<P>tgowens, I am seriously considering putting the swaybars on my kit project donor.  Eventually, I want to have something bigger than a stock 2.8L in it.  Hven't been to any Fiero runs as my schedule since I picked up the hobby in October has been no less than crazy.<P>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 08-11-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88 Database Guy||08-11-2000||09:53 AM||||Boy Mshill, I'd sure like to get the VIN off that '88 coupe before it's gone forever.<BR>If you go back and it's still there, how about snagging the VIN and basic info on it for the '88 Fiero Database project?<P>Congrats on the Fiero Rich area you're in!<P>John Willhoff  john.willhoff@gulfaero.com<BR>(912) 898-1389||||reg||1
